meta {
  name: Update Product (PATCH)
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

patch {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/REPLACE_WITH_PRODUCT_ID
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "label": "New Label",
    "status": "Completed"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.label: isString
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-15 against a disposable scratch product
  (`WC-TEST-PATCH-001`, id `6aa98167a30ca5945169a245`, created and deleted
  in this same test run) on "David's Dev Account". `openapi_pimv3.json`
  now formally declares `PATCH /products/{identifier}` (it did not before
  this spec refresh) -- this was already empirically confirmed working in
  Phase 2 (quirks #26/#27 in `config/api-testing.config.md`), but never
  had its own dedicated `.bru` file until now.

  ## What it does
  Partial update of a product. Any subset of `ProductUpdateInputDto`
  fields may be sent; unset fields are left untouched. Returns `200` with
  the **full** updated product (all fields, not just the ones patched) --
  matches `openapi_pimv3.json`'s declared `200`, contradicts `API V3.md`'s
  stated 204-for-PATCH convention (also flagged project-wide in quirk
  #56).

  ## Key fields confirmed in this run
  - `label` and `status` both apply immediately and round-trip in the
    response.
  - The response shape here is richer than `POST`'s create-response
    (adds `assets`, `categories`, `relationships` arrays, `created_user_audit`/
    `modified_user_audit`, `product_type`) -- same shape as a plain `GET`.

  ## Related, resource-specific quirks (see config for the full list)
  - `category_ids`/other relationship-array fields reliably apply via
    `PATCH` even when silently dropped on `POST` for some resources
    (quirk #27) -- not re-tested here since this file focuses on plain
    scalar fields, but relevant if extending this request.
  - `DELETE /products/{id}/{path}` ignores `{path}` and deletes the whole
    product (quirk #31) -- this is a `PATCH`-only file; never assume the
    same subpath convention is safe for `DELETE`.
}

example {
  name: Update Product - Success
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15 against a disposable scratch product on "David's Dev Account".

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6aa98167a30ca5945169a245
    method: patch
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "label": "WC Test Patch Product Updated",
        "status": "Completed"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "assets": [],
            "attributes": {
              "amazon_ready": 0.0,
              "basic_information_completeness": 0.0,
              "english_content_completeness": 0.0,
              "google_shopping_completeness": 0.0,
              "marketing_ready": 0.0,
              "product_specifications_completeness": 0.0,
              "shopify_ready": 0.0,
              "spanish_content_completeness": 0.0,
              "website_ready": 7.14
            },
            "categories": [],
            "created": "2026-09-15T17:33:27.474000+00:00",
            "created_user_audit": {
              "type": "API",
              "user_email": "TestDH",
              "user_id": "6a96a370a3fb0431c692820d"
            },
            "id": "6aa98167a30ca5945169a245",
            "label": "WC Test Patch Product Updated",
            "modified": "2026-09-15T17:33:38.480000+00:00",
            "modified_user_audit": {
              "type": "API",
              "user_email": "TestDH",
              "user_id": "6a96a370a3fb0431c692820d"
            },
            "num_variations": 0,
            "overwritten_attributes": [],
            "product_family_id": null,
            "product_family_model_id": null,
            "product_level": 0,
            "product_type": "SINGLE",
            "relationships": [],
            "sku": "WC-TEST-PATCH-001",
            "status": "Completed"
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
